    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait, you say the dissent's arguments are \"legally flawed\" but isn't the whole point of a dissent to point out where the majority missed something important? like, if the dissent was arguing based on the concept of substantive due presence or privacy, why is that considered \"flawed\" instead of just a different way of reading the 14th amendment?",
