    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the textualist view, but isn't it kind of a stretch to say a legal argument is \"not valid\" just because it lost the vote? if a different set of justices were on the bench, those same arguments about privacy and the 14th amendment would be the law of the land. isn't it part of the legal process to debate these different frameworks rather than just dismissing them as obsolete?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
